PARITY NOTES (web LiveStatusPill.tsx → native)
===========================================================================
  • tone map     TONE[state]: live → green dot + Activity, reconnecting → amber
                 pulsing + Wifi, offline → grey + WifiOff  → LiveStatusState resolves
                 tint to Color.TS.statusSuccess/statusWarning/textMuted, glyph to SF
                 Symbol waveform.path.ecg / wifi / wifi.slash, pulse only on
                 reconnecting (web animate-pulse), reduce-motion honored.
  • relative     relative(now,lastUpdateAt): null → "—"; secs=max(0,floor((now-last)
                 /1000)); <5 "just now"; <60 "{s}s ago"; <3600 "{m}m ago"; else
                 "{h}h ago"  → LiveStatusRelative.bucket. Floor (not round) and the
                 max(0,…) clock-skew clamp verified; non-finite ⇒ justNow.
  • chip         web inline-flex rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 ring-1 bg-*/10 tabular-nums
                 → Capsule fill tint·0.1 + strokeBorder tint·0.3, gap 6, pad 10/4,
                 Font.TS.label, .monospacedDigit(). Separator "·" is a typographic
                 glyph (verbatim, aria-hidden) — same convention as BatteryPill's "%".
  • a11y         role="status" aria-live="polite" + aria-label "Live status stream:
                 {label}, updated {rel}" → one combined element, label resolved via
                 the catalog (so display text == spoken text), dot/icon/middot hidden,
                 .accessibilityAddTraits(.updatesFrequently).
  • telemetry    web is pure-presentational (emits nothing); native adds the P1/S11
                 view.opened event with the stable slug "LiveStatusPill" from .task.
